# Stack rules live with the stack (owner 2026-10-10)

Org rules are stack-agnostic. Every repo also has rules for **its own** technology:

- The repo's `AGENTS.md` carries one `## <Stack> rules` section per framework/language/tool it
  actually uses (e.g. `Astro rules`, `Java rules`, `Android rules`, `Spring Boot rules`), written
  as checkable rules: what to use, what to avoid, which test/lint/hook enforces it.
- An agent working in a repo follows the org rules **plus that repo's own stack sections** — never
  another stack's rules. Do not copy a stack section into a repo that does not use that stack.
- Starting work in a repo whose stack has no section yet: add one from that stack's official best
  practices (cite the source) before or alongside the first change, and keep it short.
- Rules that apply to every repo of a stack and are not project-specific go upstream (kit PR or
  a hub shared rule), the repo keeps only its project specifics.

Reference: `wolverine-solution-landing-page/AGENTS.md` § "Astro rules (static marketing site)".
